# Astro Web (`apps/web`)

Package: `@pcms/web`. **Astro 5 static site** — not Next.js.

## Architecture

- `output: 'static'` — build emits `dist/`; no SSR server in production
- React 19 **islands only** — interactive UI in `.tsx` with `client:*` directives in `.astro` pages
- Client state: **nanostores** (`src/stores/`) — not Zustand
- UI primitives: shadcn-style in `src/components/ui/` (Radix + CVA + Tailwind)
- Path alias: `@/*` → `src/*`

## Folder map

```
src/pages/          → routes (file-based)
src/layouts/        → BaseLayout, BlogLayout
src/components/     → islands + backoffice forms
src/utils/          → api-client, cn, content, theme
src/styles/         → global SCSS, _variables, _mixins
tests/              → Vitest suites
```

## API client

Use `src/utils/api-client.ts` for all fetch calls:
- Base URL from `PUBLIC_API_URL` (see `env.d.ts`)
- Credentials `include` for refresh-cookie auth
- Trace headers via `trace-headers.ts` when OTel is active

```typescript
// ✅ Use existing client
import { api } from '@/utils/api-client';
const posts = await api.get<Post[]>('/posts');
```

## Styling

- Tailwind with `applyBaseStyles: false` — tokens in `tailwind.config.mjs`
- SCSS: Vite auto-injects `@import "variables"; @import "mixins";`
- Use `cn()` from `@/utils/cn` for conditional classes
- Match existing fonts: Source Sans 3 + Fraunces

## Astro pages

- Fetch at build time in frontmatter for static content
- Pass data as props to layouts; hydrate React islands only where needed
- Demo fallbacks exist in blog index — check `docs/11-current-gaps.md` before removing

## Back office (`/app/*`)

- `LoginForm.tsx`, `WriteForm.tsx` in `components/backoffice/`
- Auth store: `auth-store.ts` — hydrate on `/app` mount when implementing session restore
- Stub pages (`/app/posts`, `/app/media`, `/app/settings`) need real API wiring, not copy-only changes

## Anti-patterns

- Next.js patterns (App Router, `use server`, `getServerSideProps`)
- Full-page React SPA routing inside Astro
- Direct `fetch()` bypassing `api-client` (unless build-time with explicit reason)
- New state library (Redux, Zustand) — use nanostores
- Client-side secrets — only `PUBLIC_*` env vars are safe in browser
